# Audit decision

**Disposition: PASS, CONDITIONAL on the stated mathematical hypotheses, for a PROVISIONAL / WORKING research note.** The previously blocking defect in settlement-region semantics and the high-severity BANK import defect are repaired. I did not identify another blocking logical error in the revised statements and proofs. This is **not** a claim of independent formal-machine verification, experimental evidence of basin-escape speedup, external peer review, or verified fidelity to all cited companion manuscripts.

**Artifacts reviewed:** the original 9-page `Basin_Escape_Note(3).pdf` dated 16 October 2026; the earlier `ATLAS_Basin_Escape_Audit_v0_1.md` and PDF; and the newly typeset 9-page `Basin_Escape_ATLAS_Repaired_v0_2.pdf` alongside its editable LaTeX source. The new note maintains all eleven main thematic sections. This re-audit checks the revised manuscript, not merely the editor's stated intentions.

**Review method:** manual definition-by-definition and proof-by-proof consistency check; construction of the original counterexample and rechecking it against the repaired semantics; confirmation that all original audit findings have a specific disposition; LaTeX compilation and PDF rendering inspection. No AMLD+0 federation, theorem prover, chess engine, or solver-performance experiment was run. No source PDF was represented as externally checked.

